      "id": 226012,
      "name": "FearLord",
      "username": "FearLord",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/5f8ce5/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2019-03-19T08:50:16.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Mint. Also won on Chronoranger’s 4th turn. The Environment is mostly fairly helpful, and it’s fairly straightforward to take Apostate down while keeping Relics out of play. This did flag up to me that Concecrated Ground MUST destroy an ongoing or environment card, even if there are only friendly ongoing in play, so that was interesting.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>With hind sight, it quickly became clear that you could luck into some really optimal moves, but I don’t actually think it was too important - it’s fairly straightforward to win even without the most efficient plays.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
